   "seed": 1851315659,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1938629691,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "\u2022 A sync took EU CT numbers a person typed and fetched each trial's record and documents in one step. CTIS was the only source with code; which documents to fetch\n   was a command-line flag.\n\u2022 CTIS lists 12,905 trials (POST /search, up to 500 per request): the whole list takes about 30 requests. The evidence does not: a record and its PDFs are several\n   requests per trial at one per second, then the page text must be read.\n\u2022 A check that reads a trial whose documents did not all arrive, or could not be read, would call missing evidence \"not reported\": a false accusation.\n\u2022 Other registries (ClinicalTrials.gov) and trials entered by hand must fit the same flow. Nothing is in production: one current config per source, runs log the\n   one they used (ADR-004's rule).",
   "originalText": "\u2022 A sync took EU CT numbers a person typed and fetched each trial's record and documents in one step. CTIS was the only source with code; which documents to fetch\n   was a command-line flag.\n\u2022 CTIS lists 12,905 trials (POST /search, up to 500 per request): the whole list takes about 30 requests. The evidence does not: a record and its PDFs are several\n   requests per trial at one per second, then the page text must be read.\n\u2022 A check that reads a trial whose documents did not all arrive, or could not be read, would call missing evidence \"not reported\": a false accusation.\n\u2022 Other registries (ClinicalTrials.gov) and trials entered by hand must fit the same flow. Nothing is in production: one current config per source, runs log the\n   one they used (ADR-004's rule).",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": "adr-context",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
