   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "adr-decision-text",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 46,
   "y": 1335.0,
   "width": 1488,
   "height": 220.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1272189415,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 2023913385,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "We choose B: every source is registered with an adapter and a config, and trials come in in two stages; a check runs only on a trial whose evidence came in\ncompletely. B is the only option that keeps checks off missing evidence (risk, quality) and records why each trial came in (traceability).\n1. Registry: core.source gains adapter (code in src/trialwatch/sources/registry.py), enabled and config (jsonb, checked by the adapter). CTIS: listing.criteria\n   (its search fields) and page_size; evidence.document_kinds. Manual is a source with no list.\n2. Sync the list (`source sync`): page through the source's list in key order; each trial is matched by its key and identifiers, or created; core.source_listing\n   keeps its title, the day the source last changed it and the listed row. A complete pass marks the trials no longer listed (kept).\n3. Transfer evidence (`source transfer`): for chosen trials (keys, or pending / failed / stale / listed): the record, the configured documents and their page\n   text. core.evidence_transfer says complete, or failed and why. Stale: the source changed the trial since; still checkable, and shown.\n4. Only complete trials are checked: evidence.run, the CLI and the web interface refuse the others (core.ready_trials). A trial entered by hand is complete once\n   its uploads are read.\n5. Both stages are ingest runs (kind list or transfer) that log the config they used; a job can be stopped between trials. `ctis sync` is gone.",
   "originalText": "We choose B: every source is registered with an adapter and a config, and trials come in in two stages; a check runs only on a trial whose evidence came in\ncompletely. B is the only option that keeps checks off missing evidence (risk, quality) and records why each trial came in (traceability).\n1. Registry: core.source gains adapter (code in src/trialwatch/sources/registry.py), enabled and config (jsonb, checked by the adapter). CTIS: listing.criteria\n   (its search fields) and page_size; evidence.document_kinds. Manual is a source with no list.\n2. Sync the list (`source sync`): page through the source's list in key order; each trial is matched by its key and identifiers, or created; core.source_listing\n   keeps its title, the day the source last changed it and the listed row. A complete pass marks the trials no longer listed (kept).\n3. Transfer evidence (`source transfer`): for chosen trials (keys, or pending / failed / stale / listed): the record, the configured documents and their page\n   text. core.evidence_transfer says complete, or failed and why. Stale: the source changed the trial since; still checkable, and shown.\n4. Only complete trials are checked: evidence.run, the CLI and the web interface refuse the others (core.ready_trials). A trial entered by hand is complete once\n   its uploads are read.\n5. Both stages are ingest runs (kind list or transfer) that log the config they used; a job can be stopped between trials. `ctis sync` is gone.",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": "adr-decision",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
